; ACCEPTANCE: a signed 32-bit Win32 result comes back SIGNED.
;
; Under Win64 a C `int` result is in EAX, and writing EAX ZERO-extends into RAX.
; The generator read every result as `mov %r, rax`, so a negative `int` arrived
; as a large positive one: `MulDiv(-7, 6, 2)` is -21 in C and was 4294967275
; here. Every `HRESULT` has that shape, and for an `HRESULT` failure IS the
; negative value — so `(< hr 0)` was false on every failure.
;
; `wide-call.oro` called `MulDiv(7, 6, 2)`, printed 21 and passed, and the bug
; cannot show on a positive value. A WITNESS THAT CANNOT FAIL PROVES NOTHING —
; the containment harness learned that in August and it did not travel here.
; This one is chosen so the wrong answer and the right one print differently.
;
; It prints 1 (the result IS negative) and then 79 (-21 + 100). With the bug it
; printed 0 and 4294967375.
;
; `print-int` is not asked to print the negative itself: win/fmt.print-int
; prints a blank line for one, and is within its rights (refinements.md §6b).
; It needs `-checked`, because a host call's result has no declared range and
; ADR 0019 refuses arithmetic on it otherwise.

(use win/WinBase as w)
(use win/fmt as fmt)

(export main)

(def main (fn ()
  (let (w.MulDiv (- 0 7) 6 2) (fn (r)
    (seq (fmt.print-int (if (< r 0) 1 0))
         (fmt.print-int (+ r 100)))))))
